# ── Mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With nothing set, the app runs in DEMO mode: pages render, the emoji picker,
# the pair list and the claim check work against an empty registry, the
# launch button explains what is missing, and /api/launch/params still builds
# real Airlock calldata from the public RPC. Set the groups below one at a
# time to go live. Copy to .env.local first.

# ── Registry (Supabase) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run supabase/schema.sql once and create a public Storage bucket named
# `moji-images`. The anon key reads (RLS allows select only); the service role
# key is what the record route, the sponsor and the admin pages write with.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Wallet / auth (Privy) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Client: switches the header from the disabled login to Privy with X and
# external wallets, embedded EVM wallets for X-only users.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
# Server: lets /api/launch verify the caller's access token and read the
# linked X handle from Privy. Never exposed to the client.
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=

# ── Chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional RPC override for Robinhood Chain (4663). The default public RPC
# works; every request carries NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_USER_AGENT because that RPC
# rejects requests without a User-Agent header.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_USER_AGENT=launch-lab-starter
# `mainnet` (default) or `testnet`. Claims are scoped per network so a test
# never burns a mainnet combo. Doppler is only deployed on mainnet 4663.
NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK=mainnet
# Doppler's public indexer, used for ETH prices, swap volume and chart points.
DOPPLER_INDEXER_URL=https://prod.indexer.doppler.lol/graphql

# ── Site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public origin baked into token metadata URIs (the on-chain tokenURI points
# here), share links and SKILL.md's base URL. Default http://localhost:3000.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# The course fee recipient is not an env var on purpose. It lives in
# src/config/course-fee.ts and is a default.

# ── Sponsored gas (server-only) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# A hot wallet that pays gas for launches on Robinhood Chain after the
# launcher signs the intent (POST /api/launch/sponsored). Keep only the
# budget in it. Unset = launchers pay their own gas.
SPONSOR_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Total gas the sponsor may spend in USD (default 100) and launches per UTC
# day (default 10). GET /api/launch/sponsored shows spent and remaining.
SPONSOR_BUDGET_USD=100
SPONSOR_DAILY_MAX=10

# ── Jobs and back of house (server-only) ─────────────────────────────────
# Protects /api/cron/refresh, /api/cron/scan and /api/cron/verify. Vercel
# sends it as a Bearer token (see vercel.json); call them yourself elsewhere.
CRON_SECRET=
# Gates /admin: every pool, pending fees per beneficiary, market caps, and
# Claim buttons that go live when the course fee wallet is connected.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
